{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 5, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a film that tells the story of the founding of facebook and the subsequent lawsuits that followed. the movie is directed by david fincher and written by aaron sorkin, who is known for his witty and fast paced dialogue. the film stars jesse eisenberg as mark zuckerberg, the founder of facebook, and andrew garfield as eduardo saverin, zuckerberg's friend and business partner.\n\nthe movie begins with zuckerberg, a sophomore at harvard, getting dumped by his girlfriend. this event sets off a chain reaction of events that ultimately leads to the creation of facebook. zuckerberg, along with his friends and fellow students, creates a website called facemash, which allows users to compare the photos of two students and vote on which one is more attractive. the site becomes a huge success, but also generates a lot of controversy and attention from the university administration.\n\nas the story unfolds, zuckerberg meets cameron and tyler winklevoss, two wealthy and privileged students who claim to have come up with the idea for a social networking site. they approach zuckerberg with a proposal to create a site called harvard connect, which would allow harvard students to connect with each other online. however, zuckerberg eventually decides to create his own site, which he calls thefacebook, and launches it with the help of saverin.\n\nthe film follows the rapid growth and success of facebook, as well as the legal battles that ensue between zuckerberg and the winklevoss twins, who claim that zuckerberg stole their idea. the movie also explores the complex and often tumultuous relationships between zuckerberg and his friends and business partners, including saverin and sean parker, the co-founder of napster.\n\none of the standout aspects of the film is the performances of the cast. eisenberg is excellent as zuckerberg, bringing a sense of intensity and focus to the role. garfield is also great as saverin, conveying a sense of vulnerability and loyalty. justin timberlake, who plays parker, is also impressive, bringing a sense of charm and charisma to the role.\n\nthe film's script is also noteworthy, with sorkin's dialogue being both witty and insightful. the film's pacing is quick and engaging, with fincher's direction bringing a sense of energy and tension to the story. the film's score, which was composed by trent reznor and atticus ross, is also excellent, adding a sense of depth and complexity to the story.\n\noverall, the social network is a compelling and engaging film that explores the complexities of friendship, ambition, and success. it is a must-see for anyone interested in the story of facebook and the people behind it. the film's themes and characters are well developed and nuanced, making it a thought-provoking and entertaining watch.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.0028338772244751453}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -0.06196817383170128}, {"token": " network", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.0031907858792692423}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.31946098804473877}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.0001134808044298552}, {"token": " tells", "logprob": -0.45269346237182617}, {"token": " the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " story", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.009929194115102291}, {"token": " founding", "logprob": -0.038190703839063644}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -2.3841855067985307e-07}, {"token": " facebook", "logprob": -0.00032455421751365066}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.575939416885376}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -5.960462772236497e-07}, {"token": " subsequent", "logprob": -0.6480401158332825}, {"token": " lawsuits", "logprob": -0.5861849784851074}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -1.8954096958623268e-05}, {"token": " follo